# Canonical Turtle for the protocol-derived encoding of:
#   Christoph Brunken et al. (2025). Machine Learning Interatomic Potentials: library for efficient training, model development and simulation of molecular systems.
#   arXiv (Cornell University). doi:10.48550/arxiv.2505.22397  arXiv:2505.22397v2
#
# Version read: arxiv-preprint arXiv:2505.22397v2 (sha256 bae2fccfd359a035...);
#   the DOI above is cited, numbers are those of the version read.
# Corpus rank 355 (Software/implementation). Method identity follows
#   artifacts/kg/METHODS.md (registry: artifacts/kg/methods-registry.csv).
# Generated by artifacts/scripts/encode_paper.py from artifacts/kg/encoding/specs/brunken2025.yaml.
#
# Encoding scope: the curated SPICE2 data set (filtered for bonding,
# neutral charge and forces; 1,737,896 training and 87,922 validation
# structures, 95:5 split by SMILES), the three pre-trained models
# (MACE-large, NequIP, ViSNet; 220 epochs on H100 GPUs), the MACE-medium
# comparison and the speed-optimised modified MACE, the MACE-medium model
# on curated SPICE1, and the MD speed benchmarks of Tables 2 and 6.
# Validation MAEs are shown only in Fig. 2 (gaps).

