###############################################################################
# Q11 -- Computational resources
###############################################################################

# Training took about 245 h (NequIP), 158 h (ViSNet) and 266 h (MACE) on NVIDIA H100 GPUs (App. A; the number of GPUs is not stated, so the hours are recorded as given).

###############################################################################
# Q12 -- Gaps and ambiguities (prose; not triples)
###############################################################################

# - Validation energy and force MAEs per SPICE2 subset for all five SPICE2 models are shown only in Fig. 2; no values are given in the text. The SPICE1 MACE-medium validation errors are described only as 'equivalent to MACE-OFF'.
# - per_atom_us is the printed ms per MD step divided by the stated atom count (time per atom per step). Torch + ASE timings use the authors' own Torch implementations, which they say are not representative of the original codes.
# - Author affiliations are not encoded (ORCIDs are those deposited with the DOI metadata, source: datacite).
# - Evaluation roles and data, base models, inference timings with their system sizes, and the source location of each value are recorded in the encoding input (artifacts/kg/encoding/specs/brunken2025.yaml) until the schema has terms for them.
